{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they heard moving about in the garden.</b> The voice of HaShem, and this was near evening at the time the day's breeze stirred. For we find walking applied to voice, as in \"its voice goes like a serpent\" (Jeremiah 46:22), \"the sound of the shofar going and growing very strong\" (Exodus 19:19). Rabbi Jonah the Spanish grammarian said that the meaning is 'and the man was moving about in the garden.' He also said that 'in the day you eat of it' means 'within a thousand years,' by way of derash. Others said: on the sixth day he was created and on the sixth day he died. Others said: then you will be liable to death. Others said: for there is a death of punishment, as in 'for the man doing this is a son of death' (2 Samuel 12:5). Others said: from then on it will come to pass that you will die, and they brought proof from an infant. And what seems right to me is what the ancients said, that he repented, in the sense of 'but for a moment I speak' [Job 36:2 — literally 'moment I speak']."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The closing phrase רגע אדבר is an unmarked citation of Job 36:2; translated hyper-literally as it stands in Ibn Ezra's text."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:59.295343282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}